      "content": "Here's a draft memo on workstation ergonomics that I've come up with:\n\nSubject: Maintaining a Healthy Workspace: Ergonomics Guidelines\n\nDear Team,\n\nAs we continue to work remotely, it's essential that we prioritize our physical well-being to avoid discomfort and potential long-term health issues. A well-designed workspace is crucial in preventing injuries and promoting productivity. In the spirit of our team's dedication to excellence, I'd like to share some guidelines to ensure our workstations are set up to support our comfort and health.\n\n**Monitor Height and Positioning**\n\nPosition your monitor directly in front of you, at a distance of about 20-25 inches. The top of the monitor should be at eye level or slightly below. This will help prevent straining your neck and reduce eye fatigue. A good rule of thumb is to imagine a line from the top of your monitor to the top of your head, ensuring it's parallel to the floor.\n\n**Chair Support and Posture**\n\nAdjust your chair height to ensure your feet are flat on the floor or on a footrest, with your knees at or below hip level. Maintain a straight back, with your shoulders relaxed and down. Avoid slouching or leaning forward, as this can put",
